# The pause menu plays its own music (neutral, no tracks), and a phase resumed from it is not
# entered afresh, so nothing set the music again: after one visit to the menu the tune stayed off
# until the next place. The menu now hands back what it took. Settings opened from the menu in
# between must not make it forget. (Escape closes the menu through the same ResumeFromMenu as
# Continue; a script cannot press it there, since `pause` over the menu only reports it open.)
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --silent --no-save --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Yard" --period noon

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
expect-state music tracks=4

travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
expect-state music tracks=4 filter=None

pause
wait mode MainMenu 20
expect-state music tracks=0
click menu Settings
wait mode Settings 20
pause
wait mode MainMenu 20
click menu Continue
wait mode LocationInteraction 30
expect-state music tracks=4 filter=None

quit
